{
  "$comment": "Risk Analysis: what each report is about and which scope parts apply to it (REQUIREMENTS #541). The engine (engine/risk-analysis/_shared/RA-ScopePreamble.ps1) derives the report's risk factors from its subjects and the risk-factor catalog, and generates its scope from the customer's settings and exclusions -- nothing of this is written in the report's KQL. A customer overrides one report (Pro: cfg.ItemOverride 'report-scope:<report>'; Community: report-scope.custom.json). disabled = setting (SI_DisabledAssets_RiskAnalysis decides) | exclude (the report asks about usable accounts and never shows disabled ones) | include (the disabled state is part of the finding). factors.include / factors.exclude = exceptions to the derived factor set only. stale = leave out a CI whose newest last-seen is older than SI_ActiveStaleDays -- only where the last-seen means the asset still exists (a device's check-in); never on an identity report (an identity's last-seen is its sign-in activity, so the cut removed exactly the inactive accounts those reports ask about) or a public IP report (the last-seen is Shodan's last scan, not the address going away) -- #690 (35), guarded by SIv3-NoLostRows.",
  "kind": "report-scope",
  "version": 1,
  "subjects": {
    "identity-user": {
      "class": "identity",
      "recordTypes": [
        "user"
      ],
      "$note": "users and guests"
